Project Description
This project aims to refine my Java programming skills by implementing various core concepts of the language. Through this endeavor, I will explore fundamental topics such as:

Data Structures: Utilizing collections like ArrayList, HashMap, and LinkedList to manage and manipulate data efficiently.
Algorithms: Implementing algorithms to solve common problems, including searching, sorting, and pattern matching.
Object-Oriented Programming (OOP): Applying OOP principles such as encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism to design modular and reusable code.
Exception Handling: Understanding and implementing robust error handling to create reliable applications.
File I/O: Working with input and output streams to read from and write to files.
Learning Objectives
Deepen my understanding of Java’s syntax and core libraries.
Gain practical experience in applying algorithms and data structures to solve real-world problems.
Improve my problem-solving skills and ability to think algorithmically.
Develop a portfolio of projects that showcase my Java capabilities.
Technologies Used
Java SE: Core Java features and libraries.
IDE: IntelliJ IDEA or Eclipse for development.
Version Control: Git for tracking changes and collaborating.
Future Enhancements
Explore advanced topics such as multithreading, networking, and Java frameworks (e.g., Spring).
Implement more complex projects that integrate various technologies and design patterns.
